      commentary for 2 matches.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>On the Website</strong> you enter a payment card when the
        trial starts. <strong>If you do not cancel before the trial ends, it
        automatically converts to a paid Subscription and we charge the first
        monthly payment.</strong> Before the trial starts we clearly show when
        it ends and what you will pay. We will email you a reminder 3 days
        before the trial ends.</li>
      <li><strong>In the App Store</strong> the trial is an Apple introductory
        offer. <strong>If you do not cancel at least 24 hours before the trial
        ends, Apple automatically converts it to a paid Subscription.</strong>
        You can cancel in Apple's subscription management (Section 8.2).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you do not pay after the trial, you return to the free plan. Your data
      remain and you can still read what you created.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Renewal, cancellation and refunds</h2>
    <h3>8.1. Website Subscriptions</h3>
    <p>
      The Subscription renews automatically for another month and the card is
      charged at the start of each period until you cancel. You can cancel at
      any time on the Website under My subscription. It then remains active
      until the end of the paid period and does not renew. We do not refund a
      started period, except on withdrawal under Section 16.2, termination
      under Section 15, or where the law requires it. If you delete your
      account, we cancel a Website Subscription immediately, without an
      automatic refund for unused days; your rights under Section 16 are
      unaffected. If a paying parent deletes their own account, the child retains
      access until the end of the paid period and there are no further charges.
    </p>
    <h3>8.2. App Store Subscriptions</h3>
    <p>
      The Subscription renews under Apple's rules until you cancel. You can
      cancel in your iPhone or iPad Settings, under your name in Subscriptions,
      at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. The Subscription
      then runs until the end of the paid period. You can also open
      <a href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple’s subscription management page</a>.
      <strong>Deleting the App or your Melveo account does not cancel the
      Subscription with Apple.</strong> Refunds are decided by Apple; request
      one at
      <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
      We cannot refund App Store payments. If Apple issues a refund, the
      Subscription ends with us.
    </p>
    <h3>8.3. Changing plan and price</h3>
    <p>
      Upgrading within the same family takes effect immediately. On the
      Website you pay the prorated difference for the rest of the period; in
      the App Store Apple settles the unused part. Downgrading takes effect
      from the next period. We will notify you of a Website price increase at
      least 30 days before the next payment, and you may cancel before then.
      For the App Store, Apple notifies you of price changes.
    </p>
    <h3>8.4. End of a Subscription</h3>
    <p>
      When a Subscription ends you return to the free plan. Your data remain,
      you can still read what you created, but you cannot create new paid work.
    </p>

