    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>On the Website</strong> you confirm at payment with a
        separate checkbox: I am at least 15, or I am paying as the adult
        legal guardian of a child under 15. A parent can buy for a child only from their own
        account and only with an active parent link to the child in
        Melveo.</li>
      <li><strong>A parent buying for a child</strong> concludes an agreement
        for the benefit of a third party (Section 1767 of the Czech Civil
        Code). Only the parent is the contracting party and payer. The child
        is entitled to receive the performance, that is to use the paid plan.
        Cancellation, withdrawal and complaints are the parent's matter.</li>
      <li><strong>In the App Store</strong> the user concludes the purchase
        agreement with Apple under Apple's rules. Children's purchases in
        Family Sharing, including Ask to Buy, are governed by Apple's
        rules.</li>
      <li>We show offers with a price to users aged 15 or over, based on their
        date of birth in Melveo. No purchase offer is shown if age is unknown.
        If a child under 15 nevertheless buys a Subscription in the App Store, refunds are a matter between the Apple Account holder and
